  "summary": "The distinctive silver belt tradition of the Sami people, featuring elaborate buckles, belt hooks, and buttons with symbolic motifs.",
  "description": "Characterized by heavy silver buckles, ornate belt hooks (gahpir), and decorative buttons often depicting animals, plants, and geometric patterns, these belts evolved from practical items to status symbols and wealth displays. The tradition emerged as Sami people began trading silver with Scandinavian merchants and incorporated these materials into their traditional craft.",
